# Secrets — never commit. .env.example is the only checked-in env file.
# The wildcard matters: deploys routinely produce .env.production,
# .env.vercel and similar, and those are the ones that get committed by
# accident because nobody expects them to exist.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
npm-debug.log*
# TypeScript's incremental build cache. Machine-local and rewritten by every
# `tsc` run, so tracking it put a meaningless diff in front of every commit and
# invited someone to stage a stale one over a colleague's.
*.tsbuildinfo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Downloaded OpenStreetMap extracts for the connectivity agent — hundreds of
# megabytes, rebuilt daily upstream, and reproducible from
# osm_extract.EXTRACTS. Committing them would put a stale copy of the map in
# the history forever.
.cache/
